@startuml control-flow-diagram-order-processing
title Order Processing Workflow - Main Diagram (9 nodes - under 10 limit)

' This example demonstrates sub-diagram referencing when a business process
' would exceed the 10-node limit for business process diagrams

skinparam activityBackgroundColor #FEFECE
skinparam activityBorderColor #A80036

|Customer|
start
:Submit Order;
note right
  User submits order with items
  Node count: 1 (start)
end note

|Order Processing System|
:Receive Order Request;
note right
  Node count: 2 (process step)
end note

:Execute Payment Validation;
note right
  **SUB-DIAGRAM REFERENCE**
  See: control-flow-diagram-payment-validation.puml

  This sub-process contains:
  - Validate payment method (credit card/PayPal)
  - Check payment authorization
  - Handle payment decline scenarios
  - Update payment status

  Sub-diagram nodes: 8 (under 10 limit)

  Node count: 3 (process step referencing sub-diagram)
end note

if (Payment Validated?) then (yes)
  note right
    Node count: 4 (decision point)
  end note

  :Execute Inventory Check;
  note right
    **SUB-DIAGRAM REFERENCE**
    See: control-flow-diagram-inventory-check.puml

    This sub-process contains:
    - Check item availability
    - Reserve inventory
    - Handle out-of-stock scenarios
    - Update inventory status

    Sub-diagram nodes: 7 (under 10 limit)

    Node count: 5 (process step referencing sub-diagram)
  end note

  if (Inventory Available?) then (yes)
    note right
      Node count: 6 (decision point)
    end note

    :Confirm Order;
    note right
      Node count: 7 (process step)
    end note

    |Customer|
    :Display Order Confirmation;
    note right
      Node count: 8 (process step)
    end note
    stop
    note right
      Node count: 9 (end)
    end note

  else (no)
    |Customer|
    :Display Out of Stock Message;
    stop
    note right
      Alternate end path
      (included in node count if using this branch)
    end note
  endif

else (no)
  |Customer|
  :Display Payment Error;
  stop
  note right
    Alternate end path
    (included in node count if using this branch)
  end note
endif

legend right
  **DIAGRAM NODE COUNT**: 9 nodes (under 15-node limit for all diagrams)

  **Node Breakdown**:
  - Start: 1 node
  - Process steps: 5 nodes (Receive, Execute Payment Validation, Execute Inventory Check, Confirm, Display Confirmation)
  - Decision points: 2 nodes (Payment Validated?, Inventory Available?)
  - End: 1 node (primary path stop)

  **Sub-Diagrams Referenced**: 2
  - control-flow-diagram-payment-validation.puml (8 nodes - compliant ✓)
  - control-flow-diagram-inventory-check.puml (7 nodes - compliant ✓)

  **Total Complexity**: 9 + 8 + 7 = 24 nodes across all diagrams
  **Compliant**: Each diagram individually under 15-node limit ✓
endlegend

@enduml
